From: OpenWrt local build <openwrt-local@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: retain a separate nfnetlink module

Mainline now links nfnetlink into the built-in netfilter aggregate and
uses a boolean Kconfig symbol. OpenWrt exposes the symbol as a tristate
and packages nfnetlink separately. With CONFIG_NETFILTER_NETLINK=m,
the aggregate's netfilter-m objects are not linked and all its exported
symbols disappear from conntrack and nftables modules.

Build nfnetlink as a normal module again, retaining its existing module
initialization and exit handlers and OpenWrt's package boundaries.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt local build <openwrt-local@localhost>
---
--- a/net/netfilter/Makefile
+++ b/net/netfilter/Makefile
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
 netfilter-objs := core.o nf_log.o nf_queue.o nf_sockopt.o utils.o
-netfilter-$(CONFIG_NETFILTER_NETLINK) += nfnetlink.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_NETFILTER_NETLINK) += nfnetlink.o
 
 nf_conntrack-y	:= nf_conntrack_core.o nf_conntrack_standalone.o nf_conntrack_expect.o nf_conntrack_helper.o \
 		   nf_conntrack_proto.o nf_conntrack_proto_generic.o nf_conntrack_proto_tcp.o nf_conntrack_proto_udp.o \
